  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment.",
    "Combine the rice and 3 cups water in a medium pot. Bring to a boil, cover, and cook on low for 15 minutes until the water is absorbed.",
    "Whisk the soy sauce, maple syrup, rice vinegar, cornstarch, ginger, garlic powder, and 1/4 cup water in a small saucepan.",
    "Cook the sauce over medium heat for 2 to 3 minutes, stirring, until it thickens and coats a spoon.",
    "Toss the tofu with half of the sauce in a bowl. Spread it on one half of the baking sheet.",
    "Toss the broccoli with the oil and salt. Spread it on the other half of the sheet.",
    "Bake for 20 minutes, stirring once at 10 minutes, until the tofu is browned at the edges and the broccoli is tender with browned tips.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork. Divide it among four bowls and top with tofu and broccoli.",
    "Drizzle the remaining sauce over each bowl."
